  {
    "number": 912,
    "title": "Idempotent movement ledger",
    "state": "closed",
    "draft": false,
    "merged": true,
    "created_at": "2026-07-01T02:28:00Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-07-03T09:30:00Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-03T09:30:00Z",
    "head": {
      "ref": "feat/912"
    },
    "base": {
      "ref": "main"
    },
    "changed_files": 7,
    "additions": 208,
    "deletions": 131,
    "commits": 9,
    "review_comments": 3,
    "body": "**Branch** `fix/ledger-idempotence` · **Files** 7 · **Lines** +284 −96 · **Commits** 6\n\n## Why\n\nSince the move to the event bus, the consumer replays unacknowledged messages.\nThree accounts were credited twice last week.\n\n## What was done\n\nFraming written down before starting the assistant: unique constraint on\n`event_id`, dedicated error for a replay, acknowledgement on the consumer side.\n\nThe assistant produced the package skeleton and the validation test table,\nwhich is most of the lines. Two points were taken back by hand:\n\n1. **The existence check protects nothing.** The first version did `Exists`\n   then `Insert` believing that was enough. Two concurrent consumers both get\n   through. The database constraint is what settles it, and the code has to\n   catch `23505` to say so. The comment in `Record` explains why the check\n   stays anyway.\n2. **`Cents` was a `float64`.** On an accounting ledger, no.\n\n## Review thread\n\n> **Reviewer** — `TestUniqueViolationCountsAsReplay` is missing. It is the only\n> path that matters in production.\n>\n> **Author** — True. Added, with a fake store returning an error carrying\n> `SQLState` `23505`.\n\n## Still to do\n\n`AGENTS.md` still describes the synchronous monolith and the three packages\n`api` / `store` / `billing`. None of that has matched reality since the\ndecoupling. Opened as `#918`, not picked up yet."
  },
